// =============================================================================
// Dame Halvard — Armorer.  Questline: "Shields of the Fallen" (vendor.armorer)
// Keystone: the Oathshield.  Teaches armor tiers + defense waves; rescue hook (Grom).
// Cross-vendor gate: reforging needs Borin's forge lit (vendor.forge past stage 1).
// =============================================================================
title: TalkToArmorer
---
<<if $q_armorer_stage == 0>>
    Halvard: Stand straight. That padding won't stop an orc's first swing, let alone the second.
    -> Can you plate me proper?
        Halvard: I can — if you find me salvage. There's a fallen garrison's gear out past the wall. Bring it back; don't bring back their fate.
        <<set $q_armorer_stage = 1>>
        <<command: StartQuest vendor.armorer>>
        Halvard: "Shields of the Fallen." Clear a camp and recover what's left of them.
    -> Just show me your wares.
        <<command: OpenShop "armorer">>
<<elseif $q_armorer_stage == 1>>
    Halvard: Did you recover the garrison salvage?
    -> Got it.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.armorer>>
        <<set $q_armorer_stage = 2>>
        Halvard: Good steel under the rust. Now — reforge this plate at Borin's forge. If his fire's not lit yet, light a fire under HIM first.
    -> Not yet.
        Halvard: Then the wall's still your only armor. Hurry.
<<elseif $q_armorer_stage == 2>>
    <<if $q_forge_stage >= 2>>
        Halvard: Is the plate reforged at the forge?
        -> It's reforged.
            <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.armorer>>
            <<set $q_armorer_stage = 3>>
            Halvard: Then wear it and hold the line — survive a full defense wave in it. Plate's only trust you've tested.
        -> Not yet.
            Halvard: Borin's fire is lit. No excuses.
    <<else>>
        Halvard: Borin's forge is still cold — I can't reforge plate without it. Go relight the Last Ember first.
    <<endif>>
<<elseif $q_armorer_stage == 3>>
    Halvard: Did the plate hold the line?
    -> The wave broke on it.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.armorer>>
        <<command: GiveKeystone "Oathshield">>
        <<set $q_armorer_stage = 9>>
        Halvard: Then the Oathshield is yours, and Halvard's Bulwark stands with the wall. <i>She pauses.</i> That garrison — it was Grom's old company. If any survived, they'd be in the Frost Peaks. He'd want to know.
    -> Not yet.
        Halvard: Then go bleed for it like the rest of us did.
<<else>>
    Halvard: Oathshield-bearer. The walls are stronger for you. What do you need?
    -> Browse armor (buy / sell).
        <<command: OpenShop "armorer">>
    -> Upgrade my armor.
        <<command: OpenUpgrade "armorer">>
    -> Craft some gear.
        <<command: OpenCraft "armorer">>
    -> Manage my equipment.
        <<command: OpenEquip>>
    -> That's all.
        Halvard: Stay armored.
<<endif>>
===
